I knew it more or less from the beginning :-).  (In the past, you did 
not even need the items.  I ascended my first two wizards by engraving 
Elbereth with the athame they had as initial equipment at the time, at 
the entrance and exit the of every room I passed.  New monsters created 
tended to be "compartmentalized" this way and could not attack me unless 
I went into their room. -- So it was a good thing to remove the initial 
athame from wizards and introduce the necessity of an item on the 
Elbereth square to render this kind of abuse impossible. Wizards became 
a little more difficult, but got a decent compensation within the better 
spell system.  My third one ascended without this trick.)

It *is* powerful, if you have a means of engraving durably, in fact so 
powerful that there are people refusing to use it, because they think it 
is close to cheating.  If you can write only with your fingers, it will 
hardly save your skin, however.
